 "bottleneck": {
  "slice": "collection_site=XF",
  "claim": "the image adds least here -- -0.0568 against an overall +0.0335. But the honest reading of this atlas is that THE DEFICIT IS UNIFORM and this slice is not a mechanism: only six of the ranked slice levels move more than one fold-to-fold SD (0.0542) from the overall gain, three of those are collection sites at n=27-47, and one is a fold. The two that are neither -- the middle and lowest clinical-risk tertiles -- WERE built into a component (C5, gated fusion) and it came back VOID against its own control: 0.7493 gated against 0.7502 with the strata permuted. A uniform deficit rules out, in one measurement, every component that special-cases a subpopulation.",
  "image_gain": -0.0568,
  "n_units": 44,
  "rests_on_more_than_one_unit": true,
  "selected_by": "minimum image_gain among slices clearing the declared ranking floor"
 },
